<section class="heb-intro"><span class="eyebrow">ABOUT HOMEEQUITY BANK</span><h2>HomeEquity Bank</h2><p>HomeEquity Bank offers reverse mortgage options for eligible Canadian homeowners aged 55 and over. A reverse mortgage lets you borrow against some of your home's value while continuing to live in and own your home, subject to the loan terms.</p></section>
<div class="heb-benefits"><article><span>01 / EVERYDAY FREEDOM</span><h3>Support retirement cash flow</h3><p>Explore recurring advances to help cover everyday expenses or home support.</p></article><article><span>02 / A HOME THAT WORKS</span><h3>Plan improvements or care</h3><p>Consider using a lump sum for renovations, accessibility changes or unexpected costs.</p></article><article><span>03 / PERSONAL PRIORITIES</span><h3>Explore your next goal</h3><p>Discuss debt repayment or helping family with a specialist to understand the costs and options.</p></article></div>
<partial name="_SolutionsSlider" />
<section class="panel heb-considerations"><span class="eyebrow">BEFORE YOU DECIDE</span><h2>Understand the borrowing costs.</h2><p>This is a loan secured against your home. Interest and fees apply, and unpaid interest increases the balance and reduces the equity left in your home. Repayment is generally due when you sell, move out or the last borrower dies, subject to the agreement. You must keep up property taxes, insurance, maintenance and other loan obligations.</p><p>Eligibility and available funds depend on factors including age, property and lender approval. Speak with HomeEquity Bank about current rates, terms and suitability.</p><p class="field-help">HomeEquity Bank product information is separate from the POC referral program. The illustrative $25 / $50 referral rewards are not an advertised HomeEquity Bank offer.</p><a href="https://www.homeequitybank.ca/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Visit HomeEquity Bank's official website ↗</a></section>
